    <name>
      <text>sum-geometric-sequence-i-q1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The Environment Club of a Junior School starts a tree-planting drive. The numbers of trees planted on days 1, 2, 3 and 4 are:</p>
<p>\({@t1@}, \; {@t2@}, \; {@t3@}, \; {@t4@}, \; \ldots\)</p>
<p>The numbers form a geometric progression (GP). 

<p>(a) Find the common ratio, \(r\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) Find the total number of trees planted in the first {@num@} days.</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) Write an expression for \(S_n\) for this drive. Use \(n\) in your answer.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The numbers of trees are {@t1@}, {@t2@}, {@t3@}, {@t4@}, ... This is a geometric progression (GP), because each term is multiplied by the same number.</p>

<p>(a) <strong>Common ratio:</strong></p>
<p>\[ r = \frac{ {@t2@} }{ {@t1@} } = {@ta1@} \]</p>
<p>Check: \( \frac{ {@t3@} }{ {@t2@} } = {@ta1@} \).</p>

<p>(b) <strong>Total for the first {@num@} days:</strong></p>
<p>\[ S_n = \frac{a(r^n - 1)}{r - 1} \]</p>
<p>Here \( a = {@a@} \), \( r = {@r@} \) and \( n = {@num@} \).</p>
<p>\[ S_{ {@num@} } = \frac{ {@a@}\left({@r@}^{ {@num@} } - 1\right)}{ {@r@} - 1 } = \frac{ {@a@} \times {@r^num - 1@} }{ {@r - 1@} } = {@ta2@} \]</p>
<p>A total of {@ta2@} trees were planted in the first {@num@} days.</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Expression for \(S_n\):</strong></p>
<p>Put \( a = {@a@} \) and \( r = {@r@} \) into the formula:</p>
<p>\[ S_n = \frac{ {@a@}\left({@r@}^{n} - 1\right)}{ {@r@} - 1 } \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
